According to a Handelsblatt report based on multiple sources, OpenAI CEO Sam Altman held confidential talks with German Chancellor Merz, Vice Chancellor Klingbeil, and Digital Minister Wildberger starting September 24 last year about building an AI data center in Germany with up to 1 gigawatt capacity. The project could have cost a double-digit billion dollars and involved a location near the French border to import French nuclear power and bypass Germany's high energy costs.

The project failed, at least for now, as further talks brought no progress and lacked detail. A senior official said Altman promised "the moon" before plans were pulled back, and another suspected he "simply wanted to test" the government's reaction.

